From 4682f02de00207f9d0fc49047ea92e100532d030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:44:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] An action clip can play on the legs alone
 (PlayUnitAnimation's body "lower")

`PlayUnitAnimation(unit, animId, impact, trail, trailMs, variation, recovery, "lower")`: the clip
drives the pelvis and the legs and nothing above them, so the upper body keeps whatever it was
doing (a landing's legs under a bow still drawn). Every model with an upper-body split gets a
lower-body node beside its upper-body one, masked with a new group 5, the complement of group 2:
every bone inside the upper-body subtree. A borrowed clip (another model's take, 0015) gets the
same node where the model has the mask. `"full"`, `"upper"` and the automatic choice are as they
were; a model with no split plays the whole body as before.
